WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.800
US homeowners pay three times more per watt for rooftop solar than Australians. This is First Principles Daily, episode 169. A typical American household pays about $2.53 per watt to install a rooftop system. Australia runs the same hardware and the same installation closer to $0.82 per watt. Silicon cells and the inverter do not separate those two prices. The separation sits in the stack of steps that turn a finished panel into a permitted grid tied array on an actual

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.960
roof. Those steps decide how long money stays tied up, how many people must touch the

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.140
project, and whether the installer can spread fixed costs across many jobs, or must recover

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.690
them from each one. Installers in the United States still treat each residential project as

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.490
a custom job. That job has to clear separate reviews by the local building department,

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.910
the fire marshal and the utility. The reviews want drawings, structural calculations,

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.930
stations, electrical one lines, and site visits scheduled weeks apart.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.850
Customer acquisition stacks on top of that.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:09.030
Sales teams, door-to-door canvassing, and lead generation contracts can consume 15-20% of

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.870
the contract price before any hardware is ordered.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:17.390
Financing products, insurance, and installer overhead are priced to cover the long-holding

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.690
period while permits move.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:24.550
Most authorities having jurisdiction still use paper or fragmented online portals, so

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.970
So the same documents get re-entered again and again.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:33.150
The July 2025 Boston University report found that these non-hardware items account for more

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.870
than half the final US price.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:41.050
Hardware itself, modules, inverter, racking, now costs less than the United States than

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.010
the entire Australian installed price.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.930
The physical product has followed the learning curve.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.990
The surrounding services have not.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:53.010
An installer cannot reliably forecast when a signed contract will turn into revenue.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:56.670
and that uncertainty raises the price quoted to the next customer.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:02.050
Marketing spend stays high because each project must be sold individually rather than drawn

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.370
from a steady pipeline of standardized work.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.930
The same Boston University Analysis notes that Australian installers operate under policy

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:15.010
settings that create sustained high volume, so crews stay busy and design and permitting

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:19.210
templates get amortized across dozens of nearly identical jobs each month.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:24.482
The research sources for this episode do not carry a bottom-up bill of materials for the

00:02:24.482 --> 00:02:30.722
silicon, glass, aluminum, silver paste, and encapsulants in a finished module, so a precise

00:02:30.722 --> 00:02:31.882
magic wand number.

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:36.442
The cost, if you paid only for the raw atoms, cannot be calculated from them.

00:02:37.062 --> 00:02:39.862
What those sources do show is a floor of a different kind.

00:02:40.482 --> 00:02:46.022
The July 2025 Boston University Report states that US hardware alone is already higher

00:02:46.022 --> 00:02:48.782
than the 82 cents per watt Australian total.

00:02:49.522 --> 00:02:54.322
Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratories 2024 tracking the Sun edition places the median

00:02:54.322 --> 00:03:02.442
US residential price at roughly $2.49 to $2.56 per watt before incentives, which is

00:03:02.442 --> 00:03:05.482
the ban the typical $2.53 sits in.

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:11.062
Divide that finished US price by the Australian installed cost and the first principles ratio

00:03:11.062 --> 00:03:12.902
comes out at approximately three.

00:03:12.902 --> 00:03:17.382
The gap is carried almost entirely by the stages after the factory gate.

00:03:17.942 --> 00:03:22.822
Customer acquisition, permitting, inspection, interconnection, and installer overhead and

00:03:22.822 --> 00:03:23.262
profit.

00:03:23.942 --> 00:03:28.842
Boston University attributes the Australian advantage to high-volume policy-driven demand

00:03:28.842 --> 00:03:33.342
that lets installers standardize designs and move projects through a streamlined approval

00:03:33.342 --> 00:03:33.862
process.

00:03:34.282 --> 00:03:39.802
In the United States, those steps stay fragmented across thousands of local jurisdictions, each

00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:42.042
with its own forms and its own review cadence.

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:46.362
Because the sources locate the bulk of the difference in administrative and commercial

00:03:46.362 --> 00:03:51.782
layers rather than in material or manufacturing costs, the ratio points to process and

00:03:51.782 --> 00:03:53.322
organization, not physics.

00:03:53.962 --> 00:03:58.782
If every US project could move from signed contract to energized array in the same calendar

00:03:58.782 --> 00:04:03.982
time as an Australian project, the carrying cost of capital and the risk premium built into

00:04:03.982 --> 00:04:08.202
financing would fall, and the price the installer must charge would fall with them.

00:04:08.202 --> 00:04:13.342
The ratio is measuring how much of the present price is hand-offs and waiting periods rather

00:04:13.342 --> 00:04:14.602
than atoms in the panels.

00:04:15.637 --> 00:04:21.097
The National Renewable Energy Laboratory's Solar AP Plus Point, first piloted in 2020

00:04:21.097 --> 00:04:27.317
and expanded through 2024, replaces that manual permit review with an automated code compliance

00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:27.737
check.

00:04:28.197 --> 00:04:31.017
Standardized residential systems get an instant permit.

00:04:31.577 --> 00:04:37.017
The November 2024 National Renewable Energy Laboratory Performance Review reports that projects

00:04:37.017 --> 00:04:42.317
using solar app plus finish permitting and inspection 14 and a half business days faster than

00:04:42.317 --> 00:04:48.217
traditional routes. And that roughly 15,400 authority staff hours are saved each year across

00:04:48.217 --> 00:04:53.557
participating jurisdictions. Cost reductions of 2 to 13 percent have been measured where the

00:04:53.557 --> 00:04:59.077
tool is in use. The platform is now managed by the Solar Appee Foundation and has been adopted

00:04:59.077 --> 00:05:04.497
by more than 100 authorities having jurisdiction. A wider rollout would require every jurisdiction

00:05:04.497 --> 00:05:09.437
to accept the automated checklist in place of its own plan review and to align inspection

00:05:09.437 --> 00:05:14.537
checklists with it. Where that alignment has occurred, the time-saved compounds into lower

00:05:14.537 --> 00:05:19.417
carrying costs for the installer and lower customer acquisition spend because projects

00:05:19.417 --> 00:05:24.417
close faster. The remaining hard constraint is the set of local amendments and utility

00:05:24.417 --> 00:05:29.677
interconnection rules that still sit outside the automated path. Those have to be harmonized

00:05:29.677 --> 00:05:34.277
or the tool's coverage stays partial. Even partial adoption shows the mechanism.

00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:39.377
Once the permit step shrinks from days or weeks to minutes, the installer can schedule

00:05:39.377 --> 00:05:43.777
crews with greater certainty and can shrink the sales team needed to keep the pipeline full.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:49.057
The same logic reaches interconnection studies. If utilities accept the same standardized

00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:54.917
electrical one-line that Solar AP Plus already validates, the final grid tie step shortens to.

00:05:55.577 --> 00:06:00.437
Inspection pass rates remain comparable to traditional reviews, which removes the objection

00:06:00.437 --> 00:06:02.777
that speed has to come at the expense of safety.

00:06:03.177 --> 00:06:07.977
When the dominant share of a price sits in steps that never touch atoms, the first move is

00:06:07.977 --> 00:06:10.357
to make those steps identical and machine readable.

00:06:10.977 --> 00:06:15.497
A rooftop array does not get expensive because glass and silicon forgot how to be cheap.

00:06:16.077 --> 00:06:20.337
It gets expensive because each roof is still walked through a private sequence of desks.

00:06:20.737 --> 00:06:23.897
Each desk asking for a drawing the last desk already saw.

00:06:23.897 --> 00:06:28.297
each week of silence priced into the loan and into the sales call that has to be

00:06:28.297 --> 00:06:32.537
made again. Identical means the building department, the fire marshal, and the

00:06:32.537 --> 00:06:36.677
utility are checking the same checklist against the same one line. Not three

00:06:36.677 --> 00:06:40.457
cousins of that checklist written in three different portals. Machine readable

00:06:40.457 --> 00:06:44.217
means a standardized system can clear that checklist in the time it takes to

00:06:44.217 --> 00:06:48.837
submit. The way solar appy Plus already does where a jurisdiction has agreed to

00:06:48.837 --> 00:06:53.732
let the automated path stand in for its own plan review. The second move is to

00:06:53.732 --> 00:06:57.792
measure the exact hours and the exact calendar days each of those steps consumes.

00:06:58.452 --> 00:07:02.612
So the savings can be priced into the next contract instead of left as a feeling that

00:07:02.612 --> 00:07:03.772
things got a bit quicker.

00:07:04.512 --> 00:07:06.512
Days removed are carrying cost removed.

00:07:07.112 --> 00:07:11.432
Hours the authority does not spend rereading the same packet are hours that do not have

00:07:11.432 --> 00:07:12.972
to be recovered from the homeowner.

00:07:13.512 --> 00:07:17.492
A crew that knows which morning it will be on the roof does not need the same cushion in

00:07:17.492 --> 00:07:17.912
the quote.

00:07:18.392 --> 00:07:22.672
And a pipeline of standardized jobs does not need the same share of the contract spent

00:07:22.672 --> 00:07:28.432
hunting the next signature. None of that shows up in a national average. It shows up jurisdiction by

00:07:28.432 --> 00:07:33.392
jurisdiction, in the days between signature and energization, and in the dollars that fall

00:07:33.392 --> 00:07:38.532
out of the contract when those days shrink. That is why a public ledger matters more than another

00:07:38.532 --> 00:07:43.892
national snapshot. Someone has to write down for each city that has taken the automated checklist

00:07:43.892 --> 00:07:48.852
and lined its inspections up with it. How many days came off and how many dollars came off?

00:07:48.852 --> 00:07:53.652
Whether the tool was solar AP plus or an equivalent system that does the same job.

00:07:53.952 --> 00:07:56.552
Partial coverage will keep showing up as a remainder.

00:07:57.172 --> 00:08:00.352
Local amendments and interconnection rules still outside the path.

00:08:00.912 --> 00:08:04.692
And the ledger is what tells a neighboring city whether the remainder is shrinking or

00:08:04.692 --> 00:08:05.772
simply being renamed.

00:08:06.412 --> 00:08:09.312
The signal is not a press release about being solar friendly.

00:08:09.832 --> 00:08:14.152
The signal is a city committing to that same automated checklist and that same inspection

00:08:14.152 --> 00:08:14.672
alignment.

00:08:14.672 --> 00:08:19.052
Then, leaving the before and after where the next installer and the next council can

00:08:19.052 --> 00:08:19.852
read it.

00:08:19.852 --> 00:08:23.872
Who will publish the first public ledger that shows jurisdiction by jurisdiction?

00:08:24.472 --> 00:08:28.752
How many days and dollars solar AP plus or an equivalent system actually removes?

00:08:29.372 --> 00:08:33.152
And what signal would tell us the next city has decided to run the same experiment?

00:08:33.732 --> 00:08:36.172
That's a wrap on today's first principles breakdown.

00:08:36.792 --> 00:08:39.112
The ideas travel further when you pass them on.

00:08:39.612 --> 00:08:40.912
Send this to a fellow builder.

